{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792189049,"nonce":"3wL43M3ltYKQ81pLqR+bR0Sg1Kc=","title":"Typed CFG copies every statement and condition of the body it splits","message":"TypedCfgBuilder::split_statements_in_loop pushed stmt.clone() for every plain statement and cloned every branch condition and returned expression into its blocks, so each function body existed twice while SSA construction read it, and the copy was dropped after. Full-stack profile of Lua nbody start-up at 5e8f1546 (ZYLUA_PROFILE_STARTUP=40, warm-up off, 4433 samples): split_statements_in_loop's clones 97 samples, the CFG's drop of them in lower_function 46.\n\nFix: the CFG borrows the body. TypedBasicBlock\u003c'a\u003e holds Cow\u003c'a, TypedNode\u003cTypedStatement\u003e\u003e statements and its terminator Cow\u003c'a, TypedNode\u003cTypedExpression\u003e\u003e conditions and returns: borrowed from the body where the builder only copied, owned where it makes statements (counted-loop bindings and updates, match-arm guards and pattern checks, a non-block arm body). The CFG is consumed by SSA construction inside lower_function while the body is borrowed. A match arm's body is split from a slice of its block rather than a collected copy.\n\nEquivalence: HIR dumps (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR, warm-up off) for nbody, method_call, tokenize, records, pipeline, binary_trees and official api, nextvar, locals, math, constructs (13762 module dumps), closure, goto: identical with ids masked.\n\nMac, start-up instructions, median of 3 interleaved, warm-up off:\n- Lua benchmarks (ZYLUA_PROFILE_STARTUP=10): total 11.322G -\u003e 11.072G (-2.2%); nbody -3.4%, method_call -3.4%, pipeline -2.2%; method_call footprint 20.1 -\u003e 19.0 MB.\n- Lua official (one start-up): api 5.857G -\u003e 5.532G (-5.5%), footprint 137.0 -\u003e 132.1 MB; nextvar -2.6%; locals -1.5%, footprint 202.2 (202..204) -\u003e 185.0 (184..185) MB; math -2.3%; constructs -1.4%; total -2.4%.\n- Python speed kernels (ZYPY_PROFILE_STARTUP=10): 99.497G -\u003e 98.138G (-1.37%), every kernel -0.9 to -1.6%; footprint flat.\n\nChecked: Mac compiler 805/0, embed 266/0, Python 99/0, Lua 97/0 (conformance 46/46); NUC x86-64 compiler 805/0, Lua 97/0, 22 Python kernels match CPython, 17 Lua benchmarks match PUC Lua.","files":null}]}